+- `tests/pty_tui.py` cases `x2-s2-…`, `x2-s3-…`, `x2-s4-…`, `x2-s5-…` and `x2-redirected-stdio-foreground-self-stop`:
+  each runs a plain-exec control and heimdall-proto in the same interactive bash and zsh (`zsh -f -i`) session and
+  compares stop notice, `$?`, `jobs`, typed input reaching the child, process states and leftovers (S5 also the
+  meta file). `Shell` takes an `argv` for zsh. Linux runs need an image with zsh: the harness image
+  (`HP_LINUX_PTY_IMAGE=heimdall-g02-harness:<tag> tools/linux_pty.sh …`); without zsh the zsh half is reported as
+  blocked in the case detail.
+- Red on the starting commit (darwin debug build and a linux-arm64 musl build of the same commit): S1 test exit 101
+  on both; pty S3 and S4 fail on both ("child did not resume (child T, parent S)"; "nested shell did not answer
+  after fg"). S2 and S5 pass on the starting commit too (S2 through deviation b).
+
+### Known deviations and limits
+- **S2 deviation (b)**, permitted by the task: once the launcher has stopped itself to report a stop, a third party
+  continuing only the child is invisible to it; the job stays listed stopped until `fg`/`bg`, which ends it with the
+  child's status.
+- **Redirected background jobs:** a background job whose stdio has no terminal looks exactly like S1 (own
+  non-orphaned group, no tty, not the foreground group), so a child stop there is no longer mirrored; the shell lists
+  such a job running while its child is stopped. Foreground jobs with redirected stdio are still mirrored (via
+  `/dev/tty`).
+- A SIGCONT is passed on while the child is known stopped, so after a group `fg`/`bg` the child receives SIGCONT
+  twice (harmless for the continue action; a child SIGCONT handler runs twice).
+- The terminal hand-back (S4) also applies if the child's own group took the terminal while the launcher's group
+  had other members (a nested shell as a pipeline member). It only restores what the child did itself; that layout
+  is not tested, and plain exec of it does not behave like S4 either.
+- An inherited ignored SIGCONT is left alone (K6a); then S3/S4 continue-passing is disabled.
+- Residual race (narrowed, not removed): a stale stop report can still be mirrored if the launcher is stopped and
+  continued between the final re-check and its own `kill`.
+- Unchanged from §9.4: an explicit SIGTSTP/SIGSTOP to the launcher PID stops only the launcher.
+- Windows: compile-checked only (clippy `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu`, `build.sh` windows-x64); no behaviour change.
